Input: {"question": "What sport is Doak associated with?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d00", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "Doak Campbell Stadium Doak S."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d00", "start": 30, "end": 85, "text": "Campbell Stadium (in full Bobby Bowden Field at Doak S."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d00", "start": 86, "end": 220, "text": "Campbell Stadium), popularly known as \"Doak\", is a football stadium on the campus of Florida State University in Tallahassee, Florida."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d00", "start": 221, "end": 326, "text": "It is the home field of the Florida State Seminoles football team of the Atlantic Coast Conference (ACC)."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d00", "start": 327, "end": 421, "text": "Opened 67 years ago in 1950, it was originally named Doak Campbell Stadium in honor of Doak S."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d00", "start": 422, "end": 477, "text": "Campbell, the university's president from 1941 to 1957."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d00", "start": 478, "end": 607, "text": "On November 20, 2004, the Florida Legislature added longtime head football coach Bobby Bowden to the stadium name to become Bobby"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d01", "start": 0, "end": 105, "text": "Doak Campbell Stadium | American Football Database | Fandom Start a Wiki Sign In Do n't have an account ?"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0015-4df0dc7adde5:d01", "start": 106, "end": 591, "text": "Register Sign In American Football Database Explore Main Page Discuss All Pages Community Interactive Maps Recent Blog Posts NFL AFC AFC North AFC East AFC West AFC South NFL NFC NFC North NFC East N